Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-25
Subject: Depack daopt386's in-memory TContent optimizer state
License: expat

`compiler/i386/daopt386.pas` stores per-register optimizer state in the
packed `TContent` record. Later optimizer passes in both `daopt386` and
`csopt386` dereference `MemWrite` and `StartMod` through those shared
register-content slots.

That state is in-memory-only. Keeping it packed turns those ordinary nested
accesses into packed-subobject misalignment hazards for the translated
bootstrap. Depack `TContent`; this does not change any on-disk format.

diff --git a/compiler/i386/daopt386.pas b/compiler/i386/daopt386.pas
index 724492cdb5..8a7ee607f4 100644
--- a/compiler/i386/daopt386.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/daopt386.pas
@@ -81,7 +81,13 @@ type
 {the possible states of a flag}
   TFlagContents = (F_Unknown, F_notSet, F_Set);
 
-  TContent = Packed Record
+  { was `packed record` -- depacked for the tp2cc C++ bootstrap. This is
+    in-memory optimizer state, not an on-disk format, and several later
+    optimizer passes dereference `MemWrite` / `StartMod` through these
+    per-register slots. Keeping it packed turns those ordinary nested
+    accesses into packed-subobject misalignment hazards for the translated
+    bootstrap. }
+  TContent = Record
       {start and end of block instructions that defines the
        content of this register.}
                StartMod: tai;
